{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-lb.1:000001:issue_created:sase-lb.1:b2a078c57c2530e11eaa9438ca4c402668151261bf68a93a19bb9b4892594aa9","timestamp":"2026-08-14T15:09:07Z","actor":"bbugyi200.athena.015","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"sase-lb.1","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"sase-lb.1","title":"One live agent per numbered workspace — close the monitor claim hole","status":"open","issue_type":"plan","tier":"epic","parent_id":"sase-lb","owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-08-14T15:09:07Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.athena.015","updated_at":"2026-08-14T15:09:07Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"A numbered `<project>_<N>` workspace checkout is never occupied by two live agents at once. Every process that works inside a numbered workspace holds the RUNNING-field claim for that exact number for as long as it is in there, the claim's PID is always a live process, and any code path that cannot satisfy that invariant fails loudly instead of silently running unclaimed.","notes":"","design":"plan:202608/workspace_claim_invariant.md","model":"","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","dependencies":[]}}}
